    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Photos from the Hewatt-Sagarin Transect, located in the Hopkins Marine Life Refuge, Pacific Grove, California. In 1931, a graduate student at Hopkins Marine Station (HMS), Willis G. Hewatt, took an inventory of invertebrates living along a strip of intertidal rocks 108 yards long and one yard wide. In 1993, a graduate student, Rafe Sagarin, restarted surveys of the transect and maintained them until 2015 when he was tragically killed in an accident. Surveys are continued annually with the participation of the students in the Spring Introduction to Ecology class. Photos are taken of each quadrat survey. These are photos from the Hewatt Transect taken from 2015-onwards.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Micheli, Fiorenza. Hewatt Transect quadrat photographs ( 2015 - ). Dataset (images). Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: https://purl.stanford.edu/rp047tx3069",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
